Your RDS Proxy is configured with AuthScheme: SECRETS, which means it logs into Aurora using a password pulled from Secrets Manager — IAM is only used for the Lambda-to-proxy hop, not the proxy-to-Aurora hop. The proxy has exactly one secret registered, and that secret belongs to kfb_aurora_admin. There is no secret registered for pgsi_ans00315015, so that user has no valid credential for the second hop and Aurora rejects the login. On top of that, the role almost certainly has rds_iam granted, which in this mode forces Postgres to authenticate it via PAM and reject any password the proxy presents — that's the exact error text you're seeing. The fix is to revoke rds_iam from the user, give it a SCRAM-SHA-256 password, store that in a new secret, and register that secret on the proxy. No Lambda code changes needed.
